      DTO(Data Transfer Object)     ------> Model ------>   (Data Access Object) DAO
       EmployeeDto                                                     EmployeeDao
     EmployeeInputEntity                                            EmployeeOutputEntity
                                                                       EmployeeEntity

      DTO - It always interact with client. In this we can define how we want to get the data from client.(Ex. How many fields we want to get from the client like if we have 5 field in department table and we only want 3 field, we can write the logic here.)

      Model -  Represents the actual domain object mapped to the database table.
                Annotated with @Entity.
                Contains all fields that exist in the DB table.
                Used by JPA/Hibernate for persistence.

      DAO - Encapsulates database access logic.
              Uses JpaRepository or JdbcTemplate.
              Provides CRUD operations.
              Abstracts persistence details from service layer.

 ## Flow in Practice
       1. Controller receives a request with EmployeeDTO.
       2. Service converts EmployeeDTO → Employee (Model).
       3. DAO/Repository persists Employee to DB.
       4. When fetching, DAO returns Employee → Service converts it back to EmployeeDTO → Controller sends response.


     Entity Class --> JPA Repository class--> Repository(CRUD) class --> Service class (Business Logic) --> Controller CLass

